node_modules/
dist/

# Build output that lands at the REPO ROOT, not in dist/.
# `npm run dev` makes vite-plugin-pwa write these next to package.json, and the
# Vite dep cache goes in .vite/. They were untracked but NOT ignored, which is
# one `git add -A` away from repeating the 2026-07-15 accident: main is
# SOURCE-ONLY (see CLAUDE.md) and a dist mirror got committed to it once already.
#
# Root Assets/ is listed too. CLAUDE.md warns that main still tracks a stale
# snapshot of built files there — that is now OUT OF DATE: `git ls-files Assets/`
# returns nothing, and the only tracked file left at the root is index.html,
# which is the live Vite entry, not a leftover. So root Assets/ is purely build
# output today and safe to ignore outright. Real assets belong in public/Assets/.
.vite/
/Assets/
/registerSW.js
/workbox-*.js
/manifest.webmanifest
scripts/words_alpha.txt
scripts/words_ar.txt
scripts/ar_freq.txt
.shots/
.claude/

# ── SCRATCH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One ignored home for everything that is not the project: art-pipeline output,
# throwaway scripts, screenshots, abandoned experiments. 2026-09-07: 320 MB
# across ~600 untracked paths was sitting loose in the working tree, none of it
# ignored — which is one `git add -A` away from committing 320 MB into a PUBLIC
# repo's history, permanently. (A dist mirror already got committed to main once,
# on 2026-07-15.)
#
# ⚠ NOTHING IN HERE HAS EVER BEEN COMMITTED, so git cannot restore it. Deleting
# .scratch/ is genuinely irreversible — unlike deleting a tracked file, which git
# always remembers. That is the opposite of most people's instinct and it is why
# this content was archived rather than removed.
#
# ⚠ `.scratch/public-scratch/` held things that were living inside `public/`.
# Everything in public/ is copied into dist/ by a local build, so a MANUAL
# gh-pages deploy publishes it to the live site and into the service-worker
# precache — `public/_tmp_preview/` did exactly that on 2026-08-06, putting 211
# files on production. Do not move anything back into public/ unless the app
# actually references it.
.scratch/

# Secrets and local credentials — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
**/secrets.json

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Capacitor / mobile signing (keep keystores local)
*.jks
*.keystore
android/local.properties
ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Review board GENERATED output. `review/standards.mjs` (the source) and
# `.last-review.json` (the acknowledged-state ledger CI diffs against) ARE
# tracked; these two are rebuilt by `npm run review:html` on demand.
review/findings.json
review/report.html
